        {
          "id": 426820545,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": ">OK, so if it isn't ASCII, then the hex is displayed as before?\nYes\n\n>Does the check comprise all octets, or just a portion before deciding it's printable?\nGuy implemented the feature so I'm convinced it's solid ;-)\n\n>FWIW, whichever method is employed, the actual byes, both hex and ASCII (if printable) >are available in the packet bytes pane, but that won't be there (normally) on tshark >output.\n\nSure, but the person raising the issue finds problems with that...",
